From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 20:29:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: reinit per-phy stats_list on full MAC reset

A full chip reset tears down every station without draining the
per-phy stats_list, leaving list heads pointing into freed station
memory; the next mac_work tick splices and dereferences them.
Reinitialize the lists next to the existing sta_rc_list and
twt_list reinit. stats_list comes from the tx stats rework patch,
so this fix only applies on top of it.

Fixes: SDG-2422

The same full-reset path has two more instances of this same bug
class, both reachable when the very first MCU command times out
during initial firmware bring-up, before mt76_register_device()
ever ran:

1. mt7915_mac_restart(), called from the retry loop below, calls
   mt76_txq_schedule_all() as its first action. phy->tx_list is
   only INIT_LIST_HEAD'd by mt76_phy_init(), which runs from
   registration - so on an unregistered phy it is still raw zeroed
   memory. list_empty() misreads next == NULL as non-empty,
   list_splice_init() dereferences it, and writes to address 0x8
   (the prev field of a NULL list_head), panicking the kernel from
   this function's workqueue context.

2. ieee80211_restart_hw() below queues local->restart_work, whose
   first action is flush_workqueue(local->workqueue). That is only
   set up by ieee80211_register_hw(), so on an unregistered phy this
   crashes asynchronously in a kworker:
     mutex_lock+0x14/0x58
     __flush_workqueue+0x64/0x470
     ieee80211_restart_work+0x3c/0x180 [mac80211]

Guard both the same way this patch already guards stats_list: only
touch/restart a phy that completed MT76_STATE_REGISTERED. An
already-registered phy's tx_list may hold real pending entries that
mt76_txq_schedule_all() still needs to drain, and it has a real
ieee80211_restart_work to run - so this must not fire for it.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Signed-off-by: Piotr Kubik <piotr.kubik@adtran.com>
---
 mt7915/mac.c |   18 +++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/mt7915/mac.c
+++ b/mt7915/mac.c
@@ -1335,9 +1335,10 @@ static void
 mt7915_mac_full_reset(struct mt7915_dev *dev)
 {
 	struct mt76_phy *ext_phy;
-	struct mt7915_phy *phy2;
+	struct mt7915_phy *phy, *phy2;
 	int i;
 
+	phy = &dev->phy;
 	ext_phy = dev->mt76.phys[MT_BAND1];
 	phy2 = ext_phy ? ext_phy->priv : NULL;

@@ -1358,6 +1359,12 @@ mt7915_mac_full_reset(struct mt7915_dev
 	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&dev->scs_work);
 
 	mutex_lock(&dev->mt76.mutex);
+
+	if (!test_bit(MT76_STATE_REGISTERED, &dev->mphy.state))
+		INIT_LIST_HEAD(&dev->mphy.tx_list);
+	if (ext_phy && !test_bit(MT76_STATE_REGISTERED, &ext_phy->state))
+		INIT_LIST_HEAD(&ext_phy->tx_list);
+
 	for (i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
 		if (!mt7915_mac_restart(dev))
 			break;
@@ -1375,6 +1382,10 @@ mt7915_mac_full_reset(struct mt7915_dev
 	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&dev->sta_rc_list);
 	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&dev->twt_list);
 
+	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&phy->stats_list);
+	if (phy2)
+		INIT_LIST_HEAD(&phy2->stats_list);
+
 	i = mt76_wcid_alloc(dev->mt76.wcid_mask, MT7915_WTBL_STA);
 	dev->mt76.global_wcid.idx = i;
 	dev->recovery.hw_full_reset = false;
@@ -1385,8 +1396,9 @@ mt7915_mac_full_reset(struct mt7915_dev
 	if (ext_phy)
 		ieee80211_wake_queues(ext_phy->hw);
 
-	ieee80211_restart_hw(mt76_hw(dev));
-	if (ext_phy)
+	if (test_bit(MT76_STATE_REGISTERED, &dev->mphy.state))
+		ieee80211_restart_hw(mt76_hw(dev));
+	if (ext_phy && test_bit(MT76_STATE_REGISTERED, &ext_phy->state))
 		ieee80211_restart_hw(ext_phy->hw);
 }
